  "sourceText": "All experiments\n/\nCreative tools\nEXPERIMENT 06 / CREATIVE TOOLS\nMusic arranger\n\nOne motif, many ways to make it move.\n\nCan typed musical decisions become a coherent arrangement?\n\nA LITTLE FILM. A SCORE YOU CAN SHAPE.\nGive the next scene a voice.\n\nListen to eight bars, change a phrase, and hear the scene turn.\n\nSCORE A TINY FILM\nA light appears in the distance.\nScene 2 of 4 \u00b7 bars 3\u20134\nStop\nC minor\n4/4 \u00b7 8 bars\nBPM\nPlaying bar 4 of 8\n01\nOpening\nBars 1\u20132 \u00b7 Jev choice\n02\nAn answer\nBars 3\u20134 \u00b7 Jev choice\n03\nA change\nBars 5\u20136 \u00b7 Jev choice\n04\nComing home\nBars 7\u20138 \u00b7 Jev choice\nHarmony\nCm/G\nDdim/Ab\nFm/Ab\nDdim/Ab\nAb\nFm/Ab\nDdim/Ab\nCm/G\nA5\nMELODY\nAb3\n1\n2\n3\n4\n5\n6\n7\n8\nMelody\nAir flute\nGlass bell\nSoft reed\nAnswer\nMuted pluck\nWood mallet\nKeys\nElectric keys\nQuiet organ\nPad\nVelvet pad\nSlow strings\nBass\nRound bass\nPicked bass\nDrums\nSmall drum kit\nExact timing, pitches and durations come from one score.\nSave in browser\nRestore saved\nScore JSON\nSix-track MIDI\nMake it yours\nSelect a note in the roll to edit it. Pitch steps stay in the key.\nRest\n0.125 beats\n0.25 beats\n0.5 beats\n0.75 beats\n1 beat\n1.5 beats\n2 beats\n3 beats\n4 beats\nUndo\n\nShorter durations leave silence before the next note. Held notes stop before the next onset. MIDI preserves notes, timing, velocity, instruments and mutes; its General MIDI sounds depend on your player.\n\nSTART WITH A RECORDED ARRANGEMENT\nA scene to work with\nRecorded brief\nA quiet lullaby for a rainy evening\nAn upbeat melody for a morning walk\nA mysterious tune for exploring a cave\nA cheerful theme for a tiny robot\nA slow melancholy melody for an empty station\nA playful underwater dance\nAn urgent chase through a neon city\nA warm song for coming home\nA bright sunrise. Each two-bar melody must rise overall without a final drop. Keep the pulse measured.\nA quiet farewell in shadow. Each two-bar melody should descend and settle into its lower register.\nA hopeful journey over a hill. Each two-bar melody should climb to a peak and then fall back.\nA tense dive and recovery. Each two-bar melody should dip into a valley then climb back up.\nA calm conversation by the water. Every two-bar melody needs silence between gestures and a rest at its end.\nA playful midnight chase. Use offbeat melody attacks, short rests and an active pulse in every two-bar phrase.\nArrangement to compare\nRecorded Jev choices\nProcedural rule baseline\nSeeded candidate baseline\nYour musical direction\nArrange the whole brief\n\nJev chooses the key, tempo, instrument palette and four phrases ",
